        "may"
      ],
      "text": "Information about the current status of this document, any errata, and how to provide feedback on it may be obtained at http://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7797.",
      "note": "lowercase per RFC 8174: not normative by itself, but review -- normative intent is often written without keywords"
    },
    {
      "section": "Status of This Memo",
      "line_start": 68,
      "words": [
        "must"
      ],
      "text": "Code Components extracted from this document must include Simplified BSD License text as described in Section 4.e of the Trust Legal Provisions and are provided without warranty as described in the Simplified BSD License.",
      "note": "lowercase per RFC 8174: not normative by itself, but review -- normative intent is often written without keywords"
    },
    {
      "section": "1",
      "line_start": 131,
      "words": [
        "may",
        "optional"
      ],
      "text": "This specification introduces a new JWS Header Parameter value that generalizes the JWS Signing Input computation in a manner that makes base64url-encoding the payload selectable and optional. The primary set of use cases where this enhancement may be helpful are those in which the payload may be very large and where means are already in place to enable the payload to be communicated between the parties without modifications.",
      "note": "lowercase per RFC 8174: not normative by itself, but review -- normative intent is often written without keywords"
    },
    {
      "section": "5.3",
      "line_start": 436,
      "words": [
        "must"
      ],
      "text": "When using the JWS JSON Serialization, unencoded non-detached payloads must consist of the octets of the UTF-8 encoding of a sequence of Unicode code points that are representable in a JSON string.",
      "note": "lowercase per RFC 8174: not normative by itself, but review -- normative intent is often written without keywords"
    },
    {
      "section": "7",
      "line_start": 464,
      "words": [
        "should"
      ],
      "text": "Application profiles should specify whether \"b64\" with a \"false\" value is to be used by the application in each application context or not, with it then being consistently applied in each application context.",
      "note": "lowercase per RFC 8174: not normative by itself, but review -- normative intent is often written without keywords"
    }
  ],
